id: pm-fkhdy8
title: "TOON get --fields drops an empty child collection nested inside a selected object field, while JSON keeps it"
description: "CodeRabbit review of PR 1681 (deferred). restoreRequestedEmptyItemCollections restores the empty collections an explicit get --fields selection requested at the top level of item. When a selected object field contains a scalar and an empty child array, TOON compaction still drops the nested array while JSON keeps it, so absent vs empty differs by encoding inside selected objects."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[3]: agent-ux,read-output,toon
created_at: "2026-11-07T05:21:58.835Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-08T14:41:07.559Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-08T13:44:52.039Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-08T13:44:52.039Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "TOON get --fields renders every empty collection inside selected fields, recursively, exactly as JSON delivers it; JSON, SDK and MCP output are unchanged; a spec covers a nested scalar-plus-empty-array field with a negative control"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "The get facet roots moved into the import-free src/sdk/query/get-facet-roots.ts. restoreRequestedEmptyCollections in src/core/output/output.ts restores recursively inside item and every selected facet (linked, schedule, claim_state, children, blockers). restoreEmptyCollections re-inserts each source-empty array or object at any depth around what the sparse policy kept. Array rows align by position, and rows the policy dropped are re-derived from the same policy. Nulls stay dropped and non-facet envelope keys keep the sparse policy. JSON, SDK and MCP output are unchanged."
expected_result: "TOON get --fields renders every empty collection inside selected fields, recursively, exactly as JSON delivers it"
actual_result: "pm get <id> --fields id,linked renders linked.tests: [] and linked.docs: [], and --fields id,schedule renders reminders: [] and events: []; the spec covers nested scalar-plus-empty-array fields with a negative control"
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
