comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-08T13:07:47.782Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence, branch fix/annotation-read-fidelity. Reproduced on main dbe6be164 with the built CLI. pm get <id> --fields id,linked rendered linked.files but dropped linked.tests: [] and linked.docs: []; --fields id,schedule dropped schedule.reminders: [] and schedule.events: []; JSON kept all four. The cause: restoreRequestedEmptyItemCollections restored only top-level keys of item, while linked, schedule, claim_state, children and blockers are envelope facets beside item. Fix: the facet roots moved from src/sdk/query/get.ts into src/sdk/query/get-facet-roots.ts, an import-free module the core renderer can read without loading the get command. restoreRequestedEmptyCollections now restores recursively inside item and every selected facet. restoreEmptyCollections re-inserts every source-empty array or object at any depth around what the sparse policy kept. Array rows align by position when the policy kept every row; when it dropped some, the dropped rows are re-derived from the same policy. Nulls stay dropped, as the existing sj66lm spec pins for top-level item fields. Non-facet envelope keys keep the sparse policy. JSON, SDK and MCP output are unchanged; only the TOON renderer changed. The spec covers a nested scalar-plus-empty-array field (plan_scope.paths, nested.more), facets, array-of-array rows and a negative control without the selection flag."
  "2026-11-08T14:41:07.558Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review of PR 1688, both fixed. (1) Row re-derivation now carries the preserveEmpty state the sparse policy inherited at that depth. Inside a row object the policy keeps nulls and empties, so an output_format override returning item.rows [{cells: [null, [], undefined, 'x']}] used to shift 'x' onto the null slot; it now renders null, [] and x. (2) A get --fields selection whose output projection removed item ('--fields linked.tests --output-include linked') now still restores its selected facets: restoreRequestedEmptyCollections no longer requires item to be present. Both have specs in tests/unit/core/output/annotation-read-fidelity.spec.ts."
